sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User/Browser
    participant C as React Client<br/>(port 5173)
    participant S as Node Server<br/>(port 5000)
    participant ML as ML Service FastAPI<br/>(port 8000)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL<br/>(Prisma)
    participant IO as Socket.IO

    %% ── 1. SERVER STARTUP ──────────────────────────────────────
    Note over S,ML: Server Startup
    S->>ML: spawn python main.py (child_process)
    ML-->>S: stdout: "ML Service Running"

    %% ── 2. PAGE LOAD ───────────────────────────────────────────
    Note over U,DB: Page Load — Fetch Incidents
    U->>C: Open Dashboard
    C->>S: GET /api/incidents
    activate S
    S->>DB: prisma.incident.findMany()
    DB-->>S: incidents[]
    S-->>C: 200 JSON incidents[]
    deactivate S
    C-->>U: Render incident list & map

    %% ── 3. SOCKET.IO CONNECTION ────────────────────────────────
    Note over C,IO: Real-time Setup
    C->>IO: socket.connect()
    IO-->>C: connected (socket.id)

    %% ── 4. INCIDENT REPORTING WITH VIDEO ───────────────────────
    Note over U,IO: Incident Reporting Flow
    U->>C: Fill form + upload video file
    U->>C: Click "Analyze & Submit Report"
    activate C
    C->>S: POST /api/incidents/report<br/>(multipart FormData: video, source, location, description)
    activate S
    S->>S: Multer saves video to /uploads/

    alt ML Service Available
        S->>ML: POST /analyze_video (FormData: video)
        activate ML
        ML->>ML: Save to /uploads/
        ML->>ML: VideoAnalyzer.analyze_video()
        Note over ML: Runs CrowdDetector,<br/>ViolenceDetector,<br/>SuspiciousDetector,<br/>AudioDetector per frame
        ML->>ML: Write annotated video to /outputs/
        ML-->>S: {detections[], total_frames, output_video, download_url}
        deactivate ML
    else ML Service Unavailable
        S-->>S: mlAnalysis = {detections:[], total_frames:0}
        Note over S: Continues with default<br/>severity = medium
    end

    Note over S: Classify severity:<br/>Weapon→critical, Violence→critical,<br/>Crowd→high, else→medium
    S->>DB: prisma.incident.create({type, severity, confidence, ...})
    DB-->>S: incident record
    S->>IO: io.emit("new_incident", incident)
    IO-->>C: new_incident event → update UI
    S-->>C: 200 {incidentId, type, severity, detections[], output_video, download_url}
    deactivate S
    C-->>U: Show Analysis Report + Download link
    deactivate C

    %% ── 5. LIVE FEED ────────────────────────────────────────────
    Note over U,ML: Live Camera Feed Flow
    U->>C: Click "Start Feed"
    C->>ML: POST /start_feed?source=0&type=crowd
    ML-->>C: {status: "Feed Started"}
    C->>ML: GET /video_feed (MJPEG stream via img src)
    activate ML
    ML->>ML: cv2.VideoCapture(0) — capture frames
    loop While streaming
        ML-->>C: MJPEG frame boundary
        C-->>U: Render live video frame
    end
    U->>C: Click "Stop Feed"
    C->>ML: POST /stop_feed
    ML-->>C: {status: "Feed Stopped"}
    deactivate ML

    %% ── 6. RESOLVE INCIDENT ─────────────────────────────────────
    Note over U,IO: Resolve Incident Flow
    U->>C: Click "Resolve" on incident
    C->>S: PATCH /api/incidents/:id/resolve
    activate S
    S->>DB: prisma.incident.update({status: "resolved"})
    DB-->>S: updated incident
    S->>IO: io.emit("incident_updated", incident)
    IO-->>C: incident_updated event → update UI
    S-->>C: 200 {id, status: "resolved"}
    deactivate S
    C-->>U: Incident marked as resolved
